Changes in v6:
- trace the logical-LAN registration hypercalls, and the free retry in
  that same path, with netdev_dbg() instead of counting them; they fire
  on open/close and resize, not per packet, so a permanent ethtool -S
  counter earned its keep less than a debug line does. The queue
  teardown paths are left alone: they already report failures with
  netdev_err()
- drop struct ibmveth_hcall_stats and its adapter field along with the
  counters. This patch no longer touches ibmveth.h at all
- document ibmveth_free_all_queues() return contract in kdoc:
  log-and-continue, queue_handle[] cleared regardless, and callers
  still run RX pool and DMA teardown afterward
- clarified: the body now states that queue 0's handle is stored only
  on an H_SUCCESS registration, so a failed attempt leaves no stale
  handle. Teardown clears it unconditionally, per the kdoc above
- clarified: the open-fail label walk is gone from the body rather than
  corrected. It said post-register failures enter out_unregister_queues;
  only the netif_set_real_num_rx_queues() failure does. The body now
  states just the property that matters, that post-register errors
  unwind through free_all_queues()
- clarified: the claim that ordering free_all_queues() before
  free_buffer_pools() stops PHYP retaining a registered LAN while its
  pools are released is also gone; it only held on H_SUCCESS. open()
  has allocated pools before registration since v5, which is what keeps
  a pool-fail path from having a live LAN, and the body says that
  instead

Changes in v5:
- Rename helpers to ibmveth_register_logical_lan() and
  ibmveth_free_all_queues()
- Retain single-queue registration for legacy paths

Changes in v4:
- Introduce register/free helpers in the same patch that wires their
  first open/close callers; keep subordinate-only helpers deferred
  until MQ enablement.
- Correct open/close unwind so free_all_queues() precedes
  free_buffer_pools().
- Drop the orphaned big-bang "open/close pipeline" patch from v3; that
  wiring is incremental across helper patches 3-7 instead.
